<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#mulena-mukwae">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mulena Mukwae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mulena Mukwae is the title of the royal princess who rules the southern part of Barotseland from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nalolo">Nalolo</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> king, who rules from the north. Chosen from the royal family, she has her own court, council and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomboka">Kuomboka</a> ceremony, and her role reflects the dual structure of Lozi kingship, which also gave women of the royal line real political authority.</p></div>
